# Claude Code local tooling. Session scratch is not part of the project;
# the loaded rules and commands are, so they are re-included below.
CLAUDE.md
# The !.claude/ line is load-bearing, do not delete it as redundant.
# The user's global ignore file (core.excludesFile) also lists .claude/,
# and git refuses to re-include anything whose parent directory is
# excluded, so without un-ignoring the parent first the two negations
# below silently do nothing. Then .claude/* re-ignores every child, and
# the negations re-include only what we want.
!.claude/
.claude/*
# Rules and commands are the instruction set every session actually runs
# under. Tracking them puts them in review and in history instead of
# leaving them one git clean from gone. settings.local.json, skills/,
# agents/, worktrees/ and all session scratch stay ignored via .claude/*.
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/commands/
.claudeignore
hooks/
.ci-heal/
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/
.handover.md

