# docs/distribution/ stays local scratch EXCEPT the listings register and the
# dated execution packets it points to. Those record world-checked listing
# states, exact approved copy and owner-gated submission steps and must survive
# as tracked records (a register that lives only on one machine is the
# continuity failure LEDGER.md's header records).
# A directory-level ignore blocks re-inclusion of children, hence /*.
docs/distribution/*
!docs/distribution/SUBMISSIONS.md
!docs/distribution/EDITORIAL-EXECUTION-PACKETS-2026-08-25.md
